-- examples/checks/ds-tree-holds-prov-check.rofl — ds_tree_prov_read, which keeps its witnesses and has a rule that reads the
-- `derived_by` rows of the closure: such rows are needed while the world evaluates, so the closure is rows (the Rust engine does
-- not answer it from the tree here) and each of the two rules it lowers to has made a row of it.
dstp_unmade(R) :- concludes(R, dst_within), not derived_by[$kernel](_, R, _).
alarm(dstp_unmade).
